# November 22, 2026: northern and eastern Delaware County, New York (the northwestern Catskills): Bovina, Kortright
# (Bloomville, West Kortright), Stamford and Hobart, Harpersfield, Davenport, Delhi and New Kingston, with the Parker
# 13-sided barn just over the line in Jefferson, Schoharie County. Drawn at random by tools/choose.py --state ny
# (region cat), which offered Bovina Center, New Kingston and Onteora Park; the Atlas had five places within 15 km of
# Bovina Center, and the two earlier Delaware County batches (cat_qazp, cat_fpix) worked the Pepacton, Walton and the
# county's southern half. Mostly standing country churches, hamlets and barns, two restored fire towers and an
# abandoned bluestone quarry. Sources opened in this session: Wikipedia as raw text (tools/wiki_raw.py, including the
# Delaware County Register list), and through tools/page.py HMdb.org markers, the William G. Pomeroy Foundation, the
# Bovina town historian's blog, the Watershed Post, the Daily Star (on yahoo.com), the Episcopal Diocese of Albany's
# parish pages, the Hobart Historical Society, the Catskill Scenic Trail (Catskill Revitalization Corporation), the
# Friends of Bramley Mountain Fire Tower, the Catskill Mountain Club, NYC DEP's recreation maps and list, the Historical
# Society of Middletown, the Governor's Register announcement of March 14, 2024, the Register form for the Davenport
# church (NPGallery) and the Central Plan Dairy Barns form, dcnyhistory.org, CNY Hiking, CNY News and WSKG.
